---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Can you integrate with a third-party platform we already use?",
    answer:
      "Usually, if that platform provides a usable API, webhook, export mechanism or other supported integration method. We first review its technical documentation and constraints.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can two custom systems be integrated directly?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Where both systems can expose or receive data safely, we can design a direct integration or an intermediary integration layer.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "What happens when an external API is unavailable?",
    answer:
      "The appropriate behaviour depends on the business process. Reliable integrations can use retries, queues, status tracking, fallback behaviour or manual review paths.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do integrations need ongoing maintenance?",
    answer:
      "Often, yes. External providers may change APIs, authentication methods, data structures, limits or policies, so integrations should be monitored and maintained.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKP integrate payment gateways and messaging providers?",
    answer:
      "Yes, subject to the provider, account eligibility, available APIs and applicable business or regulatory requirements.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can an integration be added to existing software without rebuilding it?",
    answer:
      "Often it can. The answer depends on the existing system architecture and whether suitable extension points, APIs or database boundaries are available.",
  },
];
---

<section class="integration-faq">
  <div class="site-container integration-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>API & integration FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before connecting systems.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="integration-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .integration-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .integration-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .integration-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .integration-faq h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .integration-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .integration-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .integration-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .integration-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .integration-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
